# MASTER BUILD PROMPT — AI SOFTWARE COMPANY OS

## 1. Product Vision

Build a production-ready web application called **AI Company OS**.

The application is a virtual software development company where multiple AI agents behave like employees.

The human user acts as the **CEO / CTO / Manager**.

The user can:

* Create companies/organizations
* Create projects
* Hire/add AI employees
* Define each employee's role
* Configure the AI model used by each employee
* Define responsibilities and permissions
* Define workflows
* Create projects and goals
* Create sprints
* Create tasks
* Assign tasks to AI employees
* Allow agents to automatically assign work to other agents
* Allow agents to wait for outputs from other agents
* Allow agents to follow up when another agent is late
* Allow agents to retry failed work
* Allow agents to escalate blockers to the human
* Monitor all agents live
* Monitor sprint delivery
* See task progress
* See agent activity
* See errors
* Receive alerts
* Approve/reject important actions
* Review code and pull requests
* See project health
* See predicted delivery dates

The application should feel like managing a real software company with employees, managers, departments, projects, sprints, tasks, meetings, communication, performance and escalation.

---

# 2. Core Principle

The system must be **event-driven and state-driven**.

Agents must NOT operate as isolated chatbots.

Every agent is an employee inside an organization.

Every agent has:

* Employee ID
* Name
* Role
* Department
* Description
* AI model
* System instructions
* Skills
* Permissions
* Working status
* Current task
* Current project
* Current sprint
* Performance history
* Activity history
* Token/cost usage
* Success/failure statistics

Agents communicate through the central **Orchestrator**.

Never allow arbitrary uncontrolled agent-to-agent communication.

All important actions must be recorded.

