# 9. Dependency-Based Workflow

This is a critical feature.

A task can depend on another task.

Example:

```text
TASK-101
Database schema
        ↓
TASK-102
Backend API
        ↓
TASK-103
Frontend UI
        ↓
TASK-104
Integration
        ↓
TASK-105
QA
        ↓
TASK-106
Security Review
        ↓
TASK-107
Deployment
```

TASK-103 must NOT start until TASK-102 produces its required output.

The system should automatically detect when dependencies are satisfied.

When TASK-102 completes:

```text
Backend Agent
      ↓
Output generated
      ↓
Orchestrator validates output
      ↓
Dependency satisfied
      ↓
Frontend Agent receives TASK-103
      ↓
Frontend Agent starts
```

