# 44. Development Rules

Before writing code:

1. Analyze the requirements.
2. Create architecture.
3. Create database schema.
4. Create API specification.
5. Create UI route structure.
6. Create task breakdown.
7. Identify dependencies.
8. Implement incrementally.

Do not attempt to generate the entire application in one giant code generation step.

Work feature-by-feature.

After every feature:

```text
Implement
 ↓
Test
 ↓
Review
 ↓
Fix
 ↓
Commit
```

Never claim something is complete unless it has been tested.

